# ============================================================================
# SILKWATER CITY  (24x20 blocks, buffer 780/1300)  tileset johto_modern
# ============================================================================
# HOOK: a canal city of silk-weavers and dyers. Two railed canals cut the
#   town into three banks (North Bank market, Lantern Island, South Bank),
#   joined by five narrow railed bridges. Both canals run off the east edge
#   and empty into the harbor town next door, so the canals are a Surf route
#   between the two maps. The Gym is BUG-type (silk moths, Ariados webs):
#   leader KAIKO, a weaver. The only bridge to the Gym is closed for the
#   Lantern Festival until you clear the festival quest on Lantern Island.
#
# DISTRICTS / BUILDINGS (door step coords in obj lines below)
#   North Bank (rows 1-6)
#     Silk Market Hall (3x2, NW)  - indoor bazaar; daily rotating stock,
#                                   sells Silk Scarf / fabric items
#     Tailor (2x2)                - outfit / bag colour shop, or move-tutor
#     Dye Works (brown roof 2x2)  - dye NPC recolours a Pokemon nickname box
#                                   or gives a Mystic Water-style hold item
#     Weavers Row guild house (3x2, NE) and two homes
#     Open-air stalls (67 kiosks on brick) - 3-4 merchant NPCs, one sells
#                                   Berries, one trades a Silcoon/Cascoon
#   Lantern Island (rows 9-13)
#     Pokemon Center + Mart (W), Canal Hotel (3x4 tower, E; rest/save NPC,
#     rooftop could be a later map), Lantern Square: brick plaza with the
#     fenced Lantern Pool at its centre (hidden item in the pool rim).
#   South Bank (rows 16-18)
#     Silkwater Gym (4x2, SW, brick forecourt), gondolier's house, two homes
#
# GAMEPLAY BEATS
#   1. Arrive from the west road onto Lantern Island; PC/Mart first.
#   2. Festival guard blocks the Gym bridge (BridgeGuard). Lantern-maker
#      in the square asks for 3 Silk threads from the market stalls.
#   3. North Bank market loop: stall trades, Market Hall, tall route north
#      to the park (map 3) via the brick avenue.
#   4. Return lanterns -> festival starts (night: lanterns, palette is
#      the nite render), guard steps aside, Gym opens.
#   5. Post-Surf: canals lead east to the harbor; hidden items on canal
#      ends; a gondolier offers a scripted canal tour.
#
# EXITS  N = brick avenue to the botanical park (map 3); W = route to the
#   wider world (suggest: new route from Goldenrod's west / Route 34 coast);
#   E = Lantern Island road to the harbor town (map 2). Canal water also
#   runs off E on rows 7-8 and 14-15.
# NOTE: block 1d is the GYM-labelled front; use 1c 0f 1d 1e only for Gyms.
# TILE GAPS: no canal corner/end pieces (canals end on trees at col 0);
#   bridges are 44/46 fence-sides so there is no arched bridge graphic;
#   no lantern/festival decoration block (use NPC sprites or a new block).
# ============================================================================
tileset johto_modern
ref GoldenrodCity
key T=05 .=01 :=06 ,=02 *=04 h=67 o=0a ~=35 n=43 u=61
key <=44 >=46 r=40 f=41 t=42 l=48 e=49 j=4a s=45 S=77 w=66 x=80 z=81
key R=18 M=1f N=19 A=10 D=17 Z=11 E=1a F=0f C=1c Q=1d W=1e P=1b O=16
key H=27 I=23 J=28 K=33 1=14 2=13 3=12 4=15 5=64 9=08 0=09
grid:
TTTTTTTTTTT::TTTTTTTTTTT
TTRMN.RN.hh::h90..RMNhTT
TTADZ.OW.hh::hOW..ADZhTT
T....s.....::..........T
T:h:h:h:h:.::.RMN..12h.T
T::h:h:h::.::.EFZ......T
T...w......::.....w...hT
Tnnn<>nnnnn<>nnnnnn<>nnn
Tuuu<>uuuuu<>uuuuuu<>uuu
T.h.....::::::::..RMN.hT
T.RNRMN.::rfft::..HIJ...
..EPADK.::<~~>::..HIJ...
T.......::luuj::..ADZ.hT
Th.x...h:S::::::h.x...hT
Tnnnnnn<>nnnnnn<>nnnnnnn
Tuuuuuu<>uuuuuu<>uuuuuuu
T.RMMN.::.RN.h...,90,,hT
T.CFQW.::.OW.h12.,OW,*.T
T:::::S::..............T
TTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTT
end
